Free the PCRE character tables when a perl = TRUE pattern fails to
compile, so the character and grep targets stop reporting
pcre2_maketables() as a leak for every invalid pattern.

R_pcre2_prepare() and R_pcre_prepare() (src/main/grep.c) build the
locale character tables into a caller-owned variable before compiling
the pattern; strsplit(), grep(), gsub(), regexpr() and regexec() free
them only after their loop over the input.  When compilation fails the
helpers free the compile context and signal "invalid regular
expression", and that error unwinds past the callers' cleanup:

    Direct leak of 1088 byte(s) in 1 object(s) allocated from:
        #0 malloc
        #1 pcre2_maketables_8
        #2 R_pcre2_prepare  src/main/grep.c:429
        #3 do_strsplit      src/main/grep.c:815

The tables are only built in non-UTF-8 mode (useBytes = TRUE, or a
non-UTF-8 locale with unmarked input), which is why the UTF-8 slots of
the harnesses never hit it.  The helpers now free the tables before
signalling.

Found by OSS-Fuzz: testcase 6104737142079488 (libFuzzer_r_character,
Direct-leak, pcre2_maketables_8 <- do_strsplit; the three-byte input
"s\\\n" is strsplit("", "\\", perl = TRUE, useBytes = TRUE)).  The
reported R-source regression range r90656:r90659 is an artifact of the
harness change in PR #41, which added the perl = TRUE strsplit slots;
the leak dates from the 2019 PCRE2 port.

Upstream status: r-devel/r-svn PR #388, filed 2026-10-20 (no Bugzilla
report yet).
Delete this patch once the fix lands in R trunk (ossfuzz.sh will report
it as already-applied in the meantime, which is harmless).

diff --git a/src/main/grep.c b/src/main/grep.c
index 52644c0954..40cecd31ec 100644
--- a/src/main/grep.c
+++ b/src/main/grep.c
@@ -439,6 +439,12 @@ R_pcre2_prepare(const char *pattern, SEXP subject, bool use_UTF8,
 	char buf[256];
 	pcre2_get_error_message(errcode, (PCRE2_UCHAR *)buf, sizeof(buf));
 	pcre2_compile_context_free(ccontext);
+	/* The tables belong to the caller, whose cleanup the error unwind
+	   skips. */
+	if (*tables) {
+	    free((void *)*tables);
+	    *tables = NULL;
+	}
 	warning(_("PCRE pattern compilation error\n\t'%s'\n\tat '%s'\n"), buf,
 	        to_native(pattern + erroffset, use_UTF8));
 	error(_("invalid regular expression '%s'"),
@@ -510,6 +516,10 @@ R_pcre_prepare(const char *pattern, SEXP subject, bool use_UTF8,
 	*tables = pcre_maketables();
     *re = pcre_compile(pattern, options, &errorptr, &erroffset, *tables);
     if (!*re) {
+	/* The tables belong to the caller, whose cleanup the error unwind
+	   skips. */
+	pcre_free((void *)*tables);
+	*tables = NULL;
 	if (errorptr)
 	    warning(_("PCRE pattern compilation error\n\t'%s'\n\tat '%s'\n"),
 	            errorptr, to_native(pattern + erroffset, use_UTF8));
